# hostapd integrated EAP server - SIM/USIM identities.
#
# The EAP method is chosen by the FIRST digit of the permanent identity (the
# 3GPP NAI decoration prefix):
#     "1" -> EAP-SIM   (2G GSM triplets)
#     "0" -> EAP-AKA   (3G/4G USIM quintuplets)
#     "6" -> EAP-AKA'  (RFC 5448, modern - what carriers use today)
# "<prefix>"* is a prefix match, so every IMSI under that method matches one line
# and hostapd skips method negotiation. Milenage vectors come from hlr_auc_gw
# (eap_sim_db); no password belongs here.
#
# The permanent identity carries the IMSI in CLEARTEXT inside EAP-Response/Identity,
# so it is trivially harvested by a passive sniffer. Subscribers below (kept verbatim
# so the identity<->credential cross-check in utils/test_lab.sh matches the "6"*
# wildcard): $IDENTITY_MGT_SIM $IDENTITY_MGT_SIM_LEAK $IDENTITY_MGT_SIM_ROGUE

# Secure client starts with an anonymous outer identity; match it to AKA' so the
# server then requests the (protected) permanent identity / accepts a pseudonym.
"anonymous"*	AKA'
"0"*	AKA
"1"*	SIM
"6"*	AKA'
